// F22 -- any identifier is a valid ###FileGeneration type; the validation is dead code.
//
// Run:
//   java -cp <runner>/target/classes:$(cat cp.txt) perf.ParseMain model.pure
// Observed: ok. The protocol records  "type": "completelyMadeUpType".
//
// FileGenerationParseTreeWalker wraps its type extraction in a catch for
// IllegalArgumentException around a substring/toLowerCase that cannot throw one, so the
// message "Generation type '...' is not supported." is unreachable. The shipped types are
// Avro, Java, Protobuf, JsonSchema, Cdm, Slang; none of them is enforced at parse time.
//
// Consequence worth stating: `FileGeneration` -- the literal token the lexer declares as the
// element keyword -- is itself accepted as a generation TYPE, which is why the positive
// fixture covers that keyword by naming an element with it. The token has no privileged
// position; the grammar rule is `identifier qualifiedName { ... }` and the walker validates
// nothing.
###FileGeneration
CompletelyMadeUpType fx::repro::Generated
{
   generationOutputPath: 'x';
}
